      "math_academy_id": "e-4104",
      "problem": "Find the solution to the equation $e^{2-4x} = 2$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we take the natural logarithm $(\\ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2-4x} & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2-4x}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ 2-4x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ -4x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx  \\approx 0.327\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
